1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:06,972
and it doesn't teach you anything new.

3
00:00:07,872 --> 00:00:10,046
It asks you to finish.

4
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:15,759
By the end you'll have played one whole evening

5
00:00:16,209 --> 00:00:20,557
in your own universe, with a list in your hand,

6
00:00:21,007 --> 00:00:24,920
and you'll know that every part of it works.

7
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:28,428
You'll also know, honestly, what doesn't.

8
00:00:29,628 --> 00:00:31,802
Don't start the game yet.

9
00:00:32,702 --> 00:00:36,615
Write down where a crew will go, in order,

10
00:00:37,065 --> 00:00:40,109
and what should happen at each place.

11
00:00:41,909 --> 00:00:44,952
I've got six rows, in two sittings.

12
00:00:45,852 --> 00:00:49,330
The relay, the Tern, and the Assay Office.

13
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:53,709
Then they save, and come back another night

14
00:00:54,159 --> 00:00:55,898
for the Bone Pile.

15
00:00:57,698 --> 00:00:59,437
I follow three rules.

16
00:01:00,337 --> 00:01:02,511
Three places make an evening.

17
00:01:03,411 --> 00:01:05,585
End a sitting somewhere safe,

18
00:01:06,035 --> 00:01:10,383
because the save keeps the system the crew is in.

19
00:01:11,283 --> 00:01:15,630
And put the save between the mystery and the fight,

20
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:19,559
so they leave knowing where to go next.

21
00:01:20,759 --> 00:01:25,976
Now, ten lines of notes at the top of the main file.

22
00:01:26,876 --> 00:01:31,659
Two slashes start a note, so the game doesn't read these.

23
00:01:32,109 --> 00:01:33,848
They're there for people.

24
00:01:35,648 --> 00:01:41,300
Who the game is for, and the three dials from the battles lecture.

25
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,809
The budget for my worst system,

26
00:01:45,259 --> 00:01:47,433
and then the two sittings.

27
00:01:49,233 --> 00:01:52,276
And the most useful part, the words.

28
00:01:53,176 --> 00:01:57,959
These are the words that have to match in two places,

29
00:01:58,409 --> 00:02:02,322
and lint can't check any of them for me.

30
00:02:03,222 --> 00:02:05,396
So when I rename something,

31
00:02:05,846 --> 00:02:09,759
this is my list of where else to go.

32
00:02:10,959 --> 00:02:14,002
There are four checks before I play.

33
00:02:14,902 --> 00:02:19,685
Lint gives the three warnings we know about, and no others.

34
00:02:20,585 --> 00:02:22,324
The save is gone,

35
00:02:22,774 --> 00:02:26,252
because a run-through starts from a new game.

36
00:02:27,152 --> 00:02:30,196
The dials say what my card says.

37
00:02:31,096 --> 00:02:34,139
And the libraries are up to date.

38
00:02:35,339 --> 00:02:40,122
Here we go, and I tick each row as it happens.

39
00:02:41,922 --> 00:02:45,400
There are three leads in the Quest Log.

40
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:50,648
On Comms, I hail the Compact and pay the levy.

41
00:02:51,548 --> 00:02:56,330
Now there's more work on offer, and the escort pays better,

42
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:58,520
so I take it.

43
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,059
On to the Tern.

44
00:03:02,959 --> 00:03:07,741
There's her card, and there's the warning from the battles lecture.

45
00:03:08,641 --> 00:03:13,424
The first lead is done, and a new step has appeared.

46
00:03:15,224 --> 00:03:16,963
Now the Assay Office.

47
00:03:17,863 --> 00:03:20,907
The escort pays out as I arrive.

48
00:03:21,807 --> 00:03:25,720
I ask about the Tern, and pay the fee.

49
00:03:26,170 --> 00:03:27,909
That closes the step,

50
00:03:28,359 --> 00:03:32,272
and it tells the crew where to go next.

51
00:03:34,072 --> 00:03:36,680
That's twelve rows, and twelve ticks.

52
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:41,359
And now I close the game, on purpose.

53
00:03:42,259 --> 00:03:48,346
This is the part of an open universe that a single mission doesn't have.

54
00:03:49,246 --> 00:03:53,593
There's the save, and I'm going to leave it alone.

55
00:03:54,793 --> 00:03:57,837
I start it with the same line,

56
00:03:58,287 --> 00:04:03,070
and we're back at the Assay Office, with the same credits.

57
00:04:03,970 --> 00:04:07,883
The Quest Log is just as I left it.

58
00:04:09,683 --> 00:04:13,596
Now for the place the Gleaners won't talk about.

59
00:04:14,496 --> 00:04:16,235
Three cards come up.

60
00:04:16,685 --> 00:04:20,598
The place, the guards, and the one I wrote.

61
00:04:22,398 --> 00:04:24,137
I count eleven ships.

62
00:04:25,037 --> 00:04:28,515
Four of them are a long way off,

63
00:04:28,965 --> 00:04:31,139
three are by the wreck,

64
00:04:31,589 --> 00:04:35,067
and four are right in front of me.

65
00:04:35,967 --> 00:04:39,011
That's the battle line from last time.

66
00:04:40,811 --> 00:04:45,159
I have to tell you something about this last row.

67
00:04:46,059 --> 00:04:48,233
When I checked this page,

68
00:04:48,683 --> 00:04:53,030
a script told the game the four ships were destroyed.

69
00:04:53,930 --> 00:04:56,104
Nobody has fought this fight.

70
00:04:57,004 --> 00:05:01,787
So this is the first time, and we'll find out together.

71
00:05:02,987 --> 00:05:06,030
There are three things to read afterward.

72
00:05:06,930 --> 00:05:09,974
The runtime log, which should be empty.

73
00:05:10,874 --> 00:05:13,483
Your ticks, every one of them.

74
00:05:14,383 --> 00:05:17,861
And your standings, which should match the page.

75
00:05:19,661 --> 00:05:22,270
And then there's one more table,

76
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:25,763
the things this universe doesn't do yet.

77
00:05:26,663 --> 00:05:29,707
It has no admiral of its own.

78
00:05:30,607 --> 00:05:33,215
A story beat can't move standing.

79
00:05:34,115 --> 00:05:37,159
Lint has three warnings that are wrong.

80
00:05:38,959 --> 00:05:41,567
None of those is your mistake.

81
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:45,076
But a writer who knows them

82
00:05:45,526 --> 00:05:49,874
writes around them, and that's why they're on the page.

83
00:05:51,074 --> 00:05:52,813
Now it's your turn,

84
00:05:53,263 --> 00:05:56,307
and this time it really is yours.

85
00:05:57,207 --> 00:06:00,250
Plan two sittings, and write your card.

86
00:06:01,150 --> 00:06:05,063
Write down what you should see before you play,

87
00:06:05,513 --> 00:06:07,252
from your own files.

88
00:06:09,052 --> 00:06:11,661
Then give it to a crew,

89
00:06:12,111 --> 00:06:14,720
sit behind them, and don't help.

90
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:19,998
That's a whole universe, and you wrote it.

91
00:06:20,898 --> 00:06:23,072
Well done, and thank you.
